course: dictionary
lesson: 193
title: Words at the airport
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An airport is a place where aeroplanes take off and land. Its buildings, called terminals, are where passengers check in, go through security and wait for their flights.
explain: Read this: «Bianca's family planned to leave for the airport at 9:00 but left at 9:25 because Mum lost her passport.» Leaving for the airport tells you the family was going somewhere by plane, so airport must be a place where flights start and end.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Zara in Johannesburg met a famous footballer at the place where aeroplanes take off and land.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: An airport is a place where aeroplanes take off and land.
fact: A terminal is a building at an airport where passengers check in and wait for their flights.
fact: At security, your bags are scanned, and some liquids are not allowed.
fact: For a flight to another country, you show your passport.
fact: Airports use 24-hour times on timetables: 14:20 means twenty past two in the afternoon.
exercise: What is an airport? | A shop that sells sweets | *A place where aeroplanes take off and land | A kind of hat | A type of bus
exercise: Bianca's family planned to leave for the airport at 9:00 but left at 9:25. How late did they leave? | 16 minutes | 2 hours | 9 hours | *25 minutes
exercise: Where do passengers check in and wait for their flights? | A sweet shop | A park | *A terminal at the airport | A bus stop
test: At an airport, what happens at security? | *Your bags are scanned | You buy a new passport | You sing a song for the guards | You get a free flight
test: A flight leaves at 14:20 and takes 2 hours 30 minutes. When does it land? (ignore time differences) | 15:50 | 17:20 | *16:50 | 12:50
exam: For a flight to another country, what must you usually show at the airport? | A pencil | A library card | A toy aeroplane | *Your passport
